  "post": {
    "caption": "AMD stock fell about 7.7% on Thursday, from $530.14 to around $489 late in the day, after short seller Hunterbrook alleged that blacklisted Chinese server maker IEIT Systems kept using newer AMD firmware. Hunterbrook is short AMD; AMD says the report misrepresents its business and that it complies with US export law.\nThe report puts AMD's 2025 China and Hong Kong billings at $7.75B (22% of sales), and a US license rule covering Singapore took effect the same day.\n\nGet this week's five, free every Saturday → link in bio.\n\n#amd #semiconductors #chipstocks #exportcontrols\n\nSources: Reuters via MarketScreener (Nov 19), Decrypt (Nov 19), The Motley Fool (Nov 19), 24/7 Wall St. (Nov 19), OfficeChai (Nov 19). Not investment advice."
